Zenify CPU migration cost tuning for the BORE tree (_cpusched=bore).

The CachyOS BORE patch collapses the sched_migration_cost declaration into a
single unconditional line and renames the surrounding guard to
CONFIG_SCHED_BORE, so the CACHY-layout override in
0003-glitched-eevdf-migration-cost.patch no longer applies. This variant layers
the same ZENIFY 250us override on top of the BORE layout.

  - sched_migration_cost: ZENIFY 250us (overrides BORE/default 500us)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -97,7 +97,11 @@
 static unsigned int normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice	= 700000ULL;
 #endif /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ZENIFY
+__read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_migration_cost	= 250000UL;
+#else
 __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_migration_cost	= 500000UL;
+#endif
 
 static int __init setup_sched_thermal_decay_shift(char *str)
 {
